    <string name="about_title">About RealityOS</string>
    <string name="about_eyebrow">AN INTELLIGENT SPATIAL MEMORY</string>
    <string name="about_problem_title">From a familiar search to an operational problem</string>
    <string name="about_problem_body">Everyone has lost time looking for keys, a remote or a tool. In workshops, warehouses and operations, the same problem slows teams down when an observation leaves with the person who made it.</string>
    <string name="about_solution_title">A shared visual memory</string>
    <string name="about_solution_body">RealityOS turns voluntary photos and video walkthroughs into persistent evidence: objects, their last verified observation, nearby context and history. A later worker can retrieve what another person saw without recording the space again.</string>
    <string name="about_difference_title">The differentiated layer</string>
    <string name="about_difference_body">Meta AI can help with personal context. RealityOS adds a workspace-owned, shared and evidence-backed operational memory: history across shifts, real supporting media and a clear “last seen” record rather than a claim that an object is still there.</string>
    <string name="about_meta_title">Powered by Meta technology</string>
    <string name="about_meta_body">Muse Spark interprets evidence and questions. SAM 3.1 can locate an object when a highlight is needed. Meta Wearables Device Access Toolkit connects compatible camera, microphone, audio and Display capabilities. Availability depends on compatible hardware and official access.</string>
    <string name="about_privacy_title">Evidence, not surveillance</string>
    <string name="about_privacy_body">Register is explicit. Query does not start a capture. RealityOS retains the evidence and labels an answer as “last seen” so people can judge its freshness.</string>
